      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__xasu__mlkem__client__apis_1ga009b4223afa377d6baad06b99a43c326" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>s32</type>
        <definition>s32 XAsu_MlkemDecapsulate</definition>
        <argsstring>(XAsu_ClientParams *ClientParamPtr, XAsu_MlkemEncapsDecapsParams *MlkemParamPtr)</argsstring>
        <name>XAsu_MlkemDecapsulate</name>
        <param>
          <type>XAsu_ClientParams *</type>
          <declname>ClientParamPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="struct_x_asu___mlkem_encaps_decaps_params" kindref="compound">XAsu_MlkemEncapsDecapsParams</ref> *</type>
          <declname>MlkemParamPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function sends a command to ASUFW to perform ML-KEM decapsulation using the provided decapsulation (secret) key and ciphertext, producing a shared secret. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ClientParamPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the XAsu_ClientParams structure which holds the client input parameters. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>MlkemParamPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the <ref refid="struct_x_asu___mlkem_encaps_decaps_params" kindref="compound">XAsu_MlkemEncapsDecapsParams</ref> structure which holds the ML-KEM decapsulation parameters.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS, if IPI request to ASU is sent successfully.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XASU_INVALID_ARGUMENT, if any argument is invalid.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XASU_INVALID_UNIQUE_ID, if the unique ID is invalid.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_FAILURE, if sending an IPI request to ASU fails.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Per FIPS 203, a ciphertext that does not match the decapsulation key yields a pseudorandom shared secret rather than an error, so that decapsulation gives an attacker no way to test ciphertexts. A successful decapsulation therefore does not mean the ciphertext was genuine. Callers must establish that through key confirmation on the derived shared secret, never by expecting a failure here. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para>Validate input parameters.</para><para>Validate ML-KEM decapsulation parameters.</para><para>Generate a unique ID and register the callback function.</para><para>Create command header.</para><para>Update request buffer and send an IPI request to ASU. </para>        </inbodydescription>
